# Impossible OS user-mode test manifest
# =====================================
#
# Deployed by `make userland` to C:\tests\usermode.manifest.
# Read by the kernel-side launcher in src/kernel/test/test_usermode.c
# (TODO-04 §3 + §4 + §8). One filename per line, `#` starts a comment,
# blank lines are ignored. Order in this file is the priority order
# WITHIN a phase -- the launcher runs smokes (phase 0) then non-smokes
# (phase 1), so a smoke listed below a correctness test still runs first.
#
# §8 test-type taxonomy: the type is inferred from the filename prefix
#   test_smoke_*.exe   -> UTEST_TYPE_SMOKE       (phase 0; FAIL aborts run)
#   test_stress_*.exe  -> UTEST_TYPE_STRESS      (phase 1; looped stress_iters times)
#   test_perf_*.exe    -> UTEST_TYPE_PERF        (phase 1; emits [PERF] lines)
#   anything else      -> UTEST_TYPE_CORRECTNESS (phase 1; default)
# An optional `type=<name>` attribute on the line overrides the
# filename-derived default, e.g.:
#   test_foo.exe type=smoke     # force `test_foo.exe` into the smoke phase
#
# To restrict the run to ONE binary, set `utest_filter=test_foo.exe`
# in boot.conf (TODO-04 §4). Glob matching is supported: `test_smoke_*.exe`.

# §8 smoke phase -- one fast-fail gate for catastrophic boot regressions.
test_smoke_boot.exe

# §1 harness self-test + correctness suites.
test_harness_smoke.exe
test_syscall.exe
test_libc.exe
test_ipc.exe
# test_process.exe forks three children for fork/exec/kill sub-tests.
# Tell the launcher's pre-flight budget check so fork-heavy binaries
# count for 1 (launcher task) + 3 (forked children) = 4 slots.
test_process.exe expects_tasks=4
test_fileio.exe
test_faultinject.exe

# §8 stress + perf phase -- run after all correctness passes.
test_stress_libc.exe
test_perf_syscall.exe
